    why: 'Empirical research consistently finds that people with a strong sense of purpose live longer, recover faster from illness, resist depression more effectively, and report higher life satisfaction. The mechanism is not simply hope — it is the cognitive integration of difficulty into a larger narrative that gives it meaning.',
