    why: 'The most intractable conflicts — political, religious, personal — are conducted entirely within the space of "wrongdoing and rightdoing," where each party is primarily defending their own moral position. Rumi\'s invitation points to the possibility of encounter that goes beneath the positions to the people holding them. This is the foundation of genuine dialogue.',
